# Release owners. Combined with the `main` branch ruleset's "Require review from Code Owners", a PR
# that touches any of these paths needs an approving review from one of them. Changing `version` in
# gradle.properties drives the tag and the release, and the other paths decide what runs, with the
# release credentials, when it does.
#
# There is intentionally no catch-all `*` rule: everything else (wrappers/*, core/*, docs, ...) stays
# unowned and does NOT require these reviewers. CODEOWNERS is last-match-wins, so keep the patterns
# below non-overlapping. Release owners are managed as the org team bloxbean/release-owners, which is
# also the reviewer of the `release` and `github-pages` environments — so an owner change is a team
# membership change, made in one place. The team must stay visible and keep write access to this
# repository, or GitHub silently ignores these entries.
#
# CODEOWNERS is read from a PR's base branch.

# This file, so the protection can't be removed without a release owner.
/.github/CODEOWNERS        @bloxbean/release-owners

# Every workflow runs with the repository's secrets once it is on a protected branch.
/.github/workflows/        @bloxbean/release-owners

# Version bump -> tag -> release.
/gradle.properties         @bloxbean/release-owners

# Build logic evaluated by the credentialed release jobs, and the Gradle distribution that runs it.
/build.gradle              @bloxbean/release-owners
/settings.gradle           @bloxbean/release-owners
/gradle/wrapper/           @bloxbean/release-owners
/gradlew                   @bloxbean/release-owners
/gradlew.bat               @bloxbean/release-owners
